<div class="policy-page shell">
  <article class="policy" aria-label="Privacy Policy">
    <div class="policy__layout">
      <nav class="policy__toc" aria-labelledby="policy-toc-title">
        <details class="policy__toc-details">
          <summary class="policy__toc-summary" id="policy-toc-title">On this page</summary>
          <ol class="policy__toc-list">
            <li><a href="#what-we-collect">What we collect</a></li>
            <li><a href="#why-we-collect-it">Why we collect it</a></li>
            <li><a href="#who-sees-it">Who sees it</a></li>
            <li><a href="#cookies">Cookies</a></li>
            <li><a href="#how-long-we-keep-it">How long we keep it</a></li>
            <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
          </ol>
        </details>
      </nav>

      <div class="policy__main">
        <header class="policy__head">
          <h1 class="page-head__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p class="page-head__lede">This policy explains what Qampus stores about you, why it stores it, and who can see it. Qampus is a course project for CCIT 106.</p>
          <p class="page-head__updated">Last updated: 28 October 2026.</p>
        </header>

        <div class="policy__body">
          <section class="policy__section" aria-labelledby="what-we-collect">
            <h2 class="policy__heading" id="what-we-collect">What we collect</h2>
            <p>Your full name, student number, email, and password hash. A profile avatar if you upload one. The tickets you take. Audit rows for sign-ins and ticket changes. One session cookie while you stay signed in. When you set a password, we check it against the Pwned Passwords service using only the first five characters of a SHA-1 hash. The password itself never leaves the server.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="policy__section" aria-labelledby="why-we-collect-it">
            <h2 class="policy__heading" id="why-we-collect-it">Why we collect it</h2>
            <p>To run the queue, to match a ticket to a student at the counter, and to keep an audit trail of sign-ins and ticket changes. We do not use your data for marketing or advertising.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="policy__section" aria-labelledby="who-sees-it">
            <h2 class="policy__heading" id="who-sees-it">Who sees it</h2>
            <p>Signed-in staff and office heads can see the name on a ticket. The public display shows ticket code, service, counter, waiting count, and updated time only. It never shows a name, email, or student number.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="policy__section" aria-labelledby="cookies">
            <h2 class="policy__heading" id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
            <p>One session cookie, named cspc_queue.sid. It is httpOnly and sameSite lax. It keeps you signed in. There are no advertising or tracking cookies.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="policy__section" aria-labelledby="how-long-we-keep-it">
            <h2 class="policy__heading" id="how-long-we-keep-it">How long we keep it</h2>
            <p>Your queue data is tied to one service day in Asia/Manila time. At the start of each new service day, any ticket still waiting, called, or being served is marked expired and does not carry over. The ticket rows stay as history and are not deleted automatically.</p>
            <p>Sign-in sessions end when you sign out or when the session expires. Expired sessions are removed during routine maintenance. Audit records of sign-ins and ticket changes are kept for 90 days, then deleted during routine maintenance. Account details stay until the CCIT office removes the account.</p>
            <p>If a record is wrong, ask the CCIT office.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="policy__section" aria-labelledby="contact">
            <h2 class="policy__heading" id="contact">Contact</h2>
            <p>Ask at the CCIT office or the service window.</p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</div>
